# main: always merge, never fast-forward

**Never** bring work into `main` with a fast-forward. No exceptions.

## Required

```bash
git checkout main
git merge <branch> --no-ff -m "Merge branch <branch> into main."
```

## Forbidden on main

- `git merge <branch>` without `--no-ff` (fast-forward)
- `git merge <branch> --ff-only`
- `git pull` on `main` when it would fast-forward a feature branch tip onto `main`
- Cherry-picking feature commits directly onto `main` instead of merging the branch
- Rebasing a feature branch onto `main` and then fast-forwarding `main` to match

## If main was fast-forwarded by mistake

Reset `main` to the pre-merge tip, then redo with `--no-ff`:

```bash
git checkout main
git reset --hard <main-before-merge>
git merge <branch> --no-ff -m "Merge branch <branch> into main."
```

## History shape on main

One merge commit per integrated branch; feature commits stay on the branch side of the merge graph.
